{"id": 112394, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 5-year-old boy is admitted to the hospital after being diagnosed with B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia.\u00a0 Treatment is being discussed with the family, including regimens with various standard chemotherapeutic drugs such as vincristine, prednisone, asparaginase, methotrexate, cyclophosphamide, and mercaptopurine.\u00a0 One of the consequences of treatment with the proposed options is the risk of developing a secondary malignancy.\u00a0 Which of the following agents confers the greatest risk for this adverse effect?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Asparaginase"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Cyclophosphamide"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Mercaptopurine"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Methotrexate"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Prednisone"}, {"label": "F", "text": "Vincristine"}], "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_t38636\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">T</mark>oxicities of common chemotherapeutic agents</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Chemotherapy agent</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Mechanism of action</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Toxicity</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Anthracyclines*</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">(eg, doxorubicin)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds with topoisomerase II to cleave DNA</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds with iron to generate free radicals</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dilated cardiomyopathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Bleomycin</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Induces free radical formation</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Pulmonary fibrosis</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Cisplatin*</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cross-links DNA to inhibit DNA synthesis</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nephrotoxicity</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Ototoxicity</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Peripheral neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Cyclophosphamide*</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cross-links DNA to inhibit DNA synthesis</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hemorrhagic cystitis</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bladder cancer</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Paclitaxel</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Inhibits microtubule disassembly</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Vincristine/</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">vinblastine</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Binds \u03b2-tubulin to inhibit microtubule formation</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neuropathy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">*Drugs that induce DNA damage also increase risk for secondary malignancy.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u00a0\u00a0</p></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient with acute leukemia will undergo chemotherapy with a combination of agents, each with its own spectrum of adverse effects.\u00a0 Of particular concern are chemotherapeutic agents that <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">induce DNA damage</strong>, as these agents significantly increase the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">risk of secondary malignancy</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cyclophosphamide</strong> is a cell-cycle nonspecific alkylating agent that is converted into phosphoramide mustard, a metabolite that induces formation of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">inter- and intrastrand DNA crosslinks</strong>.\u00a0 The extensive DNA damage inhibits replication and causes apoptosis of malignant cells.\u00a0 However, nonmalignant cells are also affected and can acquire <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">new mutations</strong>\u00a0(due to erroneous DNA repair) that contribute to development of secondary malignancies.\u00a0 For instance, DNA alterations in hematopoietic stem cells can lead to the formation of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">treatment-related myeloid neoplasms</strong>. In addition, the risk of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">bladder cancer</strong> is increased, although the mechanism likely involves toxic effects of acrolein (another cyclophosphamide metabolite) on bladder urothelial cells.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Other chemotherapeutic agents that can induce significant DNA damage in nonmalignant cells include additional alkylating agents (eg, cisplatin), <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">topoisomerase inhibitors</strong> (eg, etoposide), and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">anthracyclines</strong> (eg, doxorubicin), each of which also carries a risk of secondary malignancy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Asparaginase is an enzyme that hydrolyzes asparagine, an essential amino acid for leukemic cells.\u00a0 Without asparagine, leukemic cells cannot synthesize protein and therefore undergo apoptosis.\u00a0 Asparaginase can cause hypersensitivity reactions but not secondary malignancy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices C and D)</strong>\u00a0 Mercaptopurine and methotrexate are antimetabolites that interfere with nucleotide synthesis.\u00a0 Although these drugs may be associated with a slight increased risk of secondary malignancy, the risk is not nearly as high as with agents that directly damage DNA.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Prednisone is a glucocorticoid that can cause hypertension, hyperglycemia, and weight gain with prolonged use.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice F)</strong>\u00a0 Vincristine is a vinca alkaloid that inhibits microtubule assembly during mitosis.\u00a0 Vincristine is associated with an increased risk for peripheral neuropathy, not secondary malignancy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Chemotherapeutic drugs that induce DNA damage increase the risk for secondary malignancy (eg, treatment-related myeloid neoplasms).\u00a0 Cyclophosphamide is an alkylating agent that induces apoptosis in malignant cells via formation of DNA cross-links.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Chemotherapeutic drugs that induce DNA damage increase the risk for secondary malignancy (eg, treatment-related myeloid neoplasms).  Cyclophosphamide is an alkylating agent that induces apoptosis in malignant cells via formation of DNA cross-links.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200